==Strategy==
A single LeMurr is not terribly difficult by herself but a stack of them will chew through your front line. Having at least 3 meatshields is necessary, with [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat]] being very valuable because of the high number of Aliens. Do not attack the base before the first LeMurr spawns, as you would be facing several LeMurrs with barely any cash saved up.

==='''Chapter 1'''===
LeMurr has relatively high damage and pushes quickly, but she has [[Single Attack]], which means using plenty of meatshields is enough to lock her in place. Without the first set [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] activated, LeMurr can kill a level 24 [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] in one hit. Rather than relying on [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]] like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]], it is best to use cheap meatshields with ranged attackers such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]], if you have him, makes this stage significantly easier.

==='''Chapters 2 & 3'''===
After the boss shockwave, LeMurr will spawn on a medium rate. Bring enough meatshields to hold them in place while attackers take them down. Because she has Single Attack, you can try to sync their attacks so they always hit the same meatshield. Stacks of [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cats]] and other ranged attackers (such as Paris Cat and Drama Cats) work well behind four meatshields, with focus on quantity over quality due to the LeMurrs' high damage, e.g. Cat, Crazed Cat, Li'l Cat, Tank/Catellite. Seafarer Cat's freeze ability and high damage anti-Alien Uber Rare cats can be good support.

Alternatively, if you are getting the timed score rewards after you have completed Chapter 3, you can start the battle by saving up about 1500 and then start spamming Catellite and when you have enough money send out Awakened Bahamut and he should destroy the base before the stack of Catellites you've created gets destroyed. All-in-all, you're seeking to exploit the fact that all enemies in this stage only have single-target attacks; you absolutely must protect your attackers with swarms of sacrificial meatshields.

